{"may": [{"id": "may", "headword": "मय्", "headword_slp1": "may", "fold": "may", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-1957", "senses": [{"gloss": "मय् €1 Ā. (मयते) To go, move.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "maya": [{"id": "maya", "headword": "मय", "headword_slp1": "maya", "fold": "maya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-1957", "senses": [{"gloss": "मय a. (-यी f.) An affix used to indicate ‘made of’\n, ‘consisting or composed of’, ‘full of’; कनकमय, काष्ठमय, तेजोमय, जलमय &c.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["मयः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["mayaH"]}, {"id": "mayA", "headword": "मया", "headword_slp1": "mayA", "fold": "maya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-1957", "senses": [{"gloss": "मय + .{@-या@} Medical treatment.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}, {"id": "mAya", "headword": "माय", "headword_slp1": "mAya", "fold": "maya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-1957", "senses": [{"gloss": "माय a. Possessing magical power; नमो विश्वाय मायाय चिन्त्याचिन्त्याय\n वै नमः Mb. 13. 14. 316.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["मायः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["mAyaH"]}, {"id": "mAyA", "headword": "माया", "headword_slp1": "mAyA", "fold": "maya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-1957", "senses": [{"gloss": "माया [मा-यः बा˚ नेत्वम्]\n—1 Deceit, fraud, trick, trickery; a device, an artifice; रथचर्यास्त्रमायाभिर्मोहयित्वा\n परंतप Mb. 7. 46. 24; यो मायां कुरुते मूढः प्राणत्यागे धनादिके Pt. 1. 359.\n—2 Jugglery, witchercraft, enchantment, an illusion of magic; स्वप्नो\n नु माया नु मतिभ्रमो नु Ś. 6. 10; मायायोगविदां चैव न स्वयं कोपकारणात् Kau. A. 1. 19.\n—3 (Hence) An unreal or illusory image, a phantom, illusion, unreal apparition;\n मायां मयोद्भाव्य परीक्षितोऽसि R. 2. 62; विकृतिः किं नु भवेदियं\n नु माया Ki. 13. 4; R. 12. 74; oft. as the first member of comp. in the\n sense of ‘false’, ‘phantom’, ‘illusory’; e. g. मायावचनम् false\n words; मायामृग &c.\n—4 A political trick or artifice, diplomatic feat.\n—5 (In Vedānta phil.) Unreality, the illusion by virtue of which one\n considers the unreal universe as really existent and as distinct from the\n Supreme Spirit; मायां तु प्रकृतिं विद्यान्मायिनं तु महेश्वरम् Śvet. Up.\n—6 (In Sāṅ. phil.) The Pradhāna or Prakṛti.\n—7 Wickedness.\n—8 Pity, compassion.\n—9 N. of the mother of Buddha.\n—10 Ved. Extraordinary power, wisdom (प्रज्ञा).\n—11 (With Śaivas) One of the four snares (पाश) which entangle the soul.\n—12 N. of the city Gayā.\n—13 N. of Lakṣmī.\n—14 N. of Durgā; देवीं मायां तु श्रीकामः Bhāg. 2. 3. 3.\n—15 Skill, art; दधारैको रणे राजन् वृषसेनोऽस्त्रमायया Mb. 7. 16. 1.\n.━{@Comp.@}: मायाचार, मायात्मक, मायोपजीविन्, मायाकारः, मायाकृत्, मायाजीविन्, मायाचण, मायाजलम्, मायादः, मायादेवी, मायाधर, मायापटु, मायाप्रयोगः, मायाफलम्, मायामृगः, मायायन्त्रम्, मायायोगः, मायायोधिन्, मायारसिक, मायावसिक, मायावचनम्, मायावादः, मायाविद्, मायासुतः", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "mayaH": [{"id": "mayaH", "headword": "मयः", "headword_slp1": "mayaH", "fold": "mayaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-1957", "senses": [{"gloss": "मय + .{@-यः@}\n—1 N. of a demon, the architect of the demons. (He built the ‘three cities’\n for the demons; cf. त्रिपुर. He is also said to have built a splendid\n hall for the Pāṇḍavas); सानन्दं देवताभिर्मयपुरदहने धूर्जटिः\n पातु युष्मान् Ve. 1. 3.\n—2 A horse.\n—3 A camel.\n—4 A mule.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["मय"], "synonyms_slp1": ["maya"]}, {"id": "mAyaH", "headword": "मायः", "headword_slp1": "mAyaH", "fold": "mayaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-1957", "senses": [{"gloss": "माय + .{@-यः@}\n—1 A conjurer, juggler.\n—2 A demon, an evil spirit.\n—3 N. of Viṣṇu; L. D. B. 4 A garment; L. D. B.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["माय"], "synonyms_slp1": ["mAya"]}], "mayi": [{"id": "mayI", "headword": "मयी", "headword_slp1": "mayI", "fold": "mayi", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-1957", "senses": [{"gloss": "मय + .{@-यी@} A mare.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "mayawaH": [{"id": "mayawaH", "headword": "मयटः",